# Partially live-verified 2026-10-04: BACK on the pattern keyboard cancels
# without touching the alarm's persisted fields (confirmed - Signal still
# showed "Off" both before and after the cancel). Submitting the keyboard's
# pre-filled, already-valid text via SELECT (multitap_keyboard_submit) is
# the same submit mechanism verified end-to-end elsewhere (e.g.
# wizard_create_basic_alarm.seq's label step) - not independently re-
# verified here for a PATTERN-mode keyboard specifically.
#
# NOT live-verified: actually typing a NEW pattern (valid or invalid) via
# TOUCH on the pattern-mode keyboard's note/digit grid. See
# keyboard_label_touch_entry.seq's own header for this device's touch-only
# typing model and the geometry this file's TOUCH coordinates would need -
# pattern mode's key layout differs from the plain label keyboard's (see
# CLAUDE.md's "pattern-entry keyboard" design point: SOUND's note-letter
# grid vs. VIBE's plain digit grid), so its own coordinates need deriving
# separately before this file's TOUCH lines can be trusted.
#
# Keys: TestClearAlarms=10008, TestAlarmIndex=10009, TestAlarmHour=10010,
# TestAlarmMinute=10011, TestAlarmName=10020, TestAlarmVibeCustomPattern=10039
IMPORT ../common/wipe_and_prep.seq
APPMSG --int 10008=1 10009=0 10010=7 10011=0 --string 10020=Wakeup
SLEEP 1

TAP down
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
# Navigate to Custom (row 4 from Double's default row 1 preselect).
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT vibe_picker_custom_highlighted
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT pattern_keyboard_empty_custom

# BACK cancels - no mutation, straight back to the picker/Signal chain.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_unchanged_after_cancel --mask-rect 70x25+0+203

# Seed a valid custom vibe pattern directly via the test hook (bypassing
# TOUCH typing, per this file's own header note). Back out to the main
# list first - see common/wipe_and_prep.seq's own note on reload_ui() not
# refreshing an already-open sub-window - then reopen Signal fresh.
TAP back
SLEEP 1
TAP back
SLEEP 1
# TestAlarmVibrationEnabled=1 is also needed here - signal_draw_row shows
# "Off" whenever vibration_enabled is false regardless of the underlying
# pattern (CLAUDE.md's Signal submenu design point), and it's still false
# from this file's own earlier "Off" row selection.
#
# Pattern syntax note, live-verified the hard way: "2 1- 2 1- 2" is the OLD
# pre-STORE_SCHEMA-20 digit+dash grammar (CLAUDE.md's own Signal-submenu
# section still has this stale example) - under the CURRENT ABC-notation
# grammar "1-" isn't a valid token (rest is "z", not a trailing "-"), so it
# fails to parse and ac_vibe_pattern_parse leaves the field UNCHANGED
# (logged as a warning, not an error) rather than clearing it - confirmed
# empirically: sending this bad string left the alarm's pattern as
# whatever it was already (byte-identical to the "Short" preset from
# earlier in this file, so Signal kept reading "Short", not "(custom)").
# "3 z 1" below is valid current syntax and doesn't match any VIBE_PRESETS
# entry, so it reads back as a genuine custom pattern.
APPMSG --int 10009=0 10018=1 10038=1 --string 10039="3 z 1"
SLEEP 1
LONGPRESS select
SLEEP 1
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
TAP down
SLEEP 1
TAP select
SLEEP 1
SCREENSHOT signal_menu_custom_pattern_applied --mask-rect 70x25+0+203
